  <text>
    <body>
      <p>Alexander Mair, timber yard, is listed at 10 <ref target="civic?id=Leicester%20Street">Leicester Street</ref> from 1862. From 1867 the business is Alexander Mair and Co., and from 1870 timber and iron merchants. The yard ran through to <ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Street">Victoria Street</ref>, and the directories list it under both streets from 1872: at 10, later 8, then 1 and 2 Leicester Street, and at 5, then 1, then 218 Victoria Street.</p>
      <p>It is listed in every directory to 1925, the last year under Leicester Street, and in 1890 as coach builders' ironmongers.</p>
      <p><hi rend="italic">This entry is a machine-assisted first draft by Common Ground, written from the directory records. Please correct or add to it.</hi></p>
    </body>
